# Phase 1 – Brainstorming & Ideation

## Project Title

**Script-Controlled ACL – Restrict Record Access Based on Field Value**

## Problem Statement

In an organization, different users may need access to different records based on their department, role, or other field values. Giving all users access to every record can create security and privacy issues.

## Proposed Solution

The proposed solution is to use a **Script-Controlled Access Control List (ACL)** to restrict record access based on a specific field value. The script checks the field value of a record and determines whether the current user is allowed to access the record.

## Objective

The main objective of this project is to provide secure and controlled access to records based on predefined field values.

## Key Idea

The system will:

1. Identify the field value of a record.
2. Identify the current user.
3. Compare the user's details with the record's field value.
4. Allow access when the condition is satisfied.
5. Restrict access when the condition is not satisfied.

## Example

If a record has **Department = HR**, only authorized HR users should be able to access that record. Users from other departments should not be allowed to access it.

## Expected Outcome

The project will improve record-level security by ensuring that users can access only the records they are authorized to view based on the specified field value.
